      "side": 1,
      "message": "Crasskov does not have gpio_hdmi_sel.\nSo will not define NISSA_BOARD_HAS_HDMI_SUPPORT.\nAs a result, hdmi-related functions cannot be used.\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/nissa/include/nissa_hdmi.h;l\u003d14?q\u003dNISSA_BOARD_HAS_HDMI_SUPPORT%22",
      "parentUuid": "e181320c_19d8bdcc",
      "revId": "a8c1a2e3084bc52ea81d33527ed8d89ef697a6a3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "248d14ee_d3e4f50e",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/nissa/CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-24T23:33:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That can be changed. I suggest moving that symbol to Kconfig and setting its default from devicetree:\n\n```\nconfig NISSA_BOARD_HAS_HDMI_SUPPORT\n    bool \"Board supports HDMI sub-boards\"\n    default $(dt_nodelabel_enabled,gpio_hdmi_sel)\n    help\n      Enable board code for managing the state of HDMI connections\n      on a sub-board.\n```\n\nThen replace `NISSA_BOARD_HAS_HDMI_SUPPORT` with `CONFIG_NISSA_BOARD_HAS_HDMI_SUPPORT`. An additional build-time check for presence of `gpio_hdmi_sel` will be required for boards that lack that GPIO (conditionally omitting the cases that manipulate it).",
      "parentUuid": "9c4ef440_bf5f8eab",
      "revId": "a8c1a2e3084bc52ea81d33527ed8d89ef697a6a3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
  ]
